It is the sale season again, and Chef bought items worth a total of X rupees. The sale season discount offers are structured as follows:
• If X <= 100, no discount is applied.
• If 100 < X <= 1000, a discount of 25 rupees is applied.
• If 1000 < X <= 5000, a discount of 100 rupees is applied.
• If X > 5000, a discount of 500 rupees is applied.
Find the final amount Chef needs to pay for his shopping after the discount is applied.

#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
	int x,discount,final_price;
	scanf("%d",&x);
	if(x<=100){
	    discount=0;
	    printf("no discount\n");
	}
	else if(x>100 && x<=1000)
	    discount=25;
	else if(x>1000 && x<=5000)
	    discount=100;
	else if(x>5000)
	    discount=500;
	final_price=x-discount;
	printf("final amount chef needs to pay %d", final_price);
	return 0;

}

